[quote=Garry Newman]"Claude, port this shit to ARC9. Make no mistakes."[/quote]

[hr][/hr]
[h2]About[/h2]

A full port of the ARCCW addons [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2906702282]Urban Renewal[/url], [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2641653126]Urban Decay[/url], [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3253847737]HK USP[/url], and their shared library [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2640556672]UC Commons[/url].

This brings all 17 weapons and all of their attachments and customization to the ARC9 weapon base. 

Its still a work in progress, so bugs and some other parity issues are to be expected. I'm only one person, so chances are I missed something when I was testing this addon during development. Any feedback helps. The more detailed the feedback, the better! The goal is to have a port that functions and looks identical to the ARCCW version, but with some new ARC9 swag. 

[hr][/hr]
[h2]Source Code[/h2]

This addon is open source: [url=https://github.com/DeisDev/UC-ARC9-Port]Source Code on GitHub[/url] 

If you know the inner workings of ARC9 or ARCCW well, any contributions to this port would always be appreciated!

I'd prefer bug reports as [url=https://github.com/DeisDev/UC-ARC9-Port/issues/new?template=bug_report.yml]GitHub issues[/url]. 

I also know a good amount of folks have never used github before, so I also have a bug discussion thread. Putting bug reports in the discussions thread helps me immensely as it allows all the bug reports to be read in one place. Check it out [url=https://steamcommunity.com/workshop/filedetails/discussion/3812993432/587313700791306663/]HERE[/url]

[hr][/hr]
[h2]Disclaimer[/h2]

This was made for personal use, but I thought perhaps someone else would want this too. The authors of the original addons announced a little while ago that they were not going to port them to ARC9, so I did it myself. This is not endorsed by the creators of Urban Coalition.

